course: dictionary
lesson: 4677
title: Proper nouns: Hollywood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hollywood is a proper noun. A proper noun is the name of one special place or thing, so it always starts with a capital letter. Hollywood is an area of the city of Los Angeles, in California, USA.
explain: Hollywood can also mean the whole American film industry, the companies that make films. Context tells you which meaning is used. «Studies of Hollywood films report that shots have got shorter over the decades» is talking about films, so here Hollywood means the film industry, not a place.
explain: Ask yourself: is the sentence about a place, or about films and stars? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Hollywood is an area of Los Angeles in California, USA.
fact: Hollywood also means the American film industry as a whole.
fact: «A Hollywood star» is a famous film actor, and «a Hollywood film» is a big, expensive American film.
fact: A «Hollywood ending» is a happy ending.
fact: Bollywood (India) and Nollywood (Nigeria) are names for other film industries, named in the same way.
exercise: Hollywood is an area of which city? | Paris | *Los Angeles | Sydney | London
exercise: In «studies of Hollywood films report that shots have got shorter over the decades», what does Hollywood mean? | A kind of camera | *The American film industry | A town with a famous sign on a hill | A happy ending
exercise: What does «a Hollywood ending» mean? | A very long ending | *A happy ending | A sad ending | An ending in the rain
test: Which word is a proper noun that needs a capital letter? | *Hollywood | star | film | ending
test: Bollywood is a film industry named like Hollywood. Which country is it for? | *India | USA | Nigeria | California
exam: In «a Hollywood film», what does Hollywood tell you? | A type of dog | *That it is a big American film | Only a place name | A cold, wet day
